before:
An 8px top inset keeps the heading eight pixels below the scrollport’s top while scrolling.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.scroller { height: 100px; overflow: auto; } .heading { position: sticky; top: 8px; height: 24px; background: navy; color: white; } .space { height: 260px; }
```

after:
The supplied panel is 100 pixels tall and has more content below. This rule keeps its heading at the top while you scroll.
```css
.heading {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
}
```
